# Images

Use [Material images](https://squidfunk.github.io/mkdocs-material/reference/images/) for a figure on the page. This is Markdown, not the PDFormy `image` block. `attr_list`, `md_in_html`, and `pymdownx.blocks.caption` are enabled. Do not add the glightbox plugin.

```markdown
![Line chart with three points](assets/line.png){ align=left width="300" loading=lazy }
/// caption
Line chart with three points
///
```

- The text in brackets is the alt text. Say what the figure shows. Do not write "image" or leave it empty.
- The path is relative to the Markdown file. Keep the file under `docs/`.
- The site palette is `default` and `slate`, so a light and a dark version use the same alt text and a hash on the URL:

```markdown
![Line chart with three points](assets/line.png#only-light)
![Line chart with three points](assets/line-dark.png#only-dark)
```

- `align` is `left` or `right`. There is no centered alignment. A `/// caption` block centers the figure on its own.
- `width` is a pixel width. `loading=lazy` defers an image below the fold.
- On a narrow page an aligned image becomes full width, so do not depend on text sitting beside it.
